@ventilators_2020
# prose-audit: Grade C — The contract, the intermediary and the undelivered machines are concrete and the audit route is visibly locked behind the 2019–20 NIK decision; the hospital that never received the ventilators is a category rather than a place.
title: The ventilator contract
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 32
order: 20
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2020 and month = 5 and ventilators_2020_done = 0
subtitle: An emergency purchase, an arms dealer and machines that never arrive
face-image: img/poland/events/hospital-ward.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.ventilators_2020_done = 1;
Q.pis_poll_momentum = (Number(Q.pis_poll_momentum) || 0) - 0.45;
Q.covid_procurement_exposure =
    (Number(Q.covid_procurement_exposure) || 0) + 25;
Q.administrative_reform_pressure =
    (Number(Q.administrative_reform_pressure) || 0) + 4;
Q.institutional_trust = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) - 4
);
Q.news_headline =
    "The health ministry's emergency ventilator contract goes to an arms dealer";
!}

= May 2020 — Thirty-five million for machines that did not come

In the first weeks of the pandemic the health ministry transferred roughly
thirty-five million złoty, in advance and without a tender, to a small firm
whose owner is an arms dealer with no medical supply history. A fraction of the
ventilators arrived. Some of those were unusable. Most of the money did not
come back.

Emergency procurement law permitted the speed. Nothing permitted the choice of
counterparty, and every hospital director who spent that spring rationing
equipment now has a number to compare against their own requisition forms.

[? if covid_policy = "Restrictions with a social shield": We supported the
restrictions on condition that the state protect people through them, which
makes this our bill to present as well as theirs.?]
[? if covid_policy = "Constitutional emergency": We said in March that a lawful
state of natural disaster would have brought rules, records and compensation
with it. This is the argument arriving in invoice form.?]
[? if covid_policy = "National unity": We offered the government temporary
unity in March. The photographs of that offer will be used against every
sentence we now say about its procurement.?]
[? if covid_policy = "Proportionality opposition": We opposed the restrictions
as disproportionate, and the government will answer that we would have spent
the money on nothing at all.?]

- @vent20_nik_referral
- @vent20_procurement_rule
- @vent20_health_workers
- @vent20_scandal

@vent20_nik_referral
title: Refer the contract to the audit chamber
subtitle: Requires an open referral channel. Produces a statutory finding with document access no parliamentary question can obtain.
choose-if: nik_referral_channel = 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no channel into the Supreme Audit Office — that was decided in November 2019 and again in January 2020.
on-arrival: {!
Q.procurement_scandal_stance = "Audit referral";
Q.covid_procurement_exposure =
    (Number(Q.covid_procurement_exposure) || 0) + 20;
Q.nik_government_hostility =
    (Number(Q.nik_government_hostility) || 20) + 10;
Q.institutional_trust = (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) + 5;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 3;
Q.administrative_reform_pressure =
    (Number(Q.administrative_reform_pressure) || 0) + 4;
Q.media_capacity = (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) + 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The audit chamber opens the emergency-procurement file";
!}

The referral goes in with dates, transfers and the ministry officials who
signed. The chamber has powers we do not: it can demand the contract, the
bank confirmations and the internal correspondence, and it can publish what it
finds without asking a minister's permission.

This is the difference between an accusation and a finding. The accusation
lasts a news cycle; the finding sits in a public register for the rest of the
parliament and is quoted by every journalist who comes to the subject later.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@vent20_procurement_rule
title: Write the emergency-procurement transparency rule
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Fixes the next emergency instead of this one; the current money stays gone.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: No policy staff are free to draft a procurement standard.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources = (Number(Q.resources) || 0) - 1;
Q.procurement_scandal_stance = "Procurement standard";
Q.emergency_procurement_standard = 1;
Q.administrative_reform_pressure =
    (Number(Q.administrative_reform_pressure) || 0) + 7;
Q.institutional_trust = (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) + 4;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "A published emergency-procurement standard follows the ventilator money";
!}

Speed and secrecy are not the same thing. Our draft keeps every emergency
power the ministry used and adds three obligations: publish the counterparty
within seven days, record who authorised the advance, and report delivery
against payment.

None of it returns the thirty-five million. All of it means the next crisis
produces a record while the crisis is happening, which is the only moment at
which such a record can still change what somebody buys.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@vent20_health_workers
title: Take the number to the wards that were rationing equipment
subtitle: Makes the scandal about the people who worked the spring without it; slower than an accusation and harder to dismiss.
on-arrival: {!
Q.procurement_scandal_stance = "Ward-level campaign";
Q.health_policy_pressure =
    (Number(Q.health_policy_pressure) || 0) + 6;
Q.labor_credibility = (Number(Q.labor_credibility) || 0) + 4;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 4;
Q.local_network = (Number(Q.local_network) || 0) + 2;
Q.covid_procurement_exposure =
    (Number(Q.covid_procurement_exposure) || 0) + 8;
Q.news_headline =
    "Nurses and hospital directors put the ventilator money beside their requisition forms";
!}

We do not hold the press conference in Warsaw. We hold it with nurses, an
anaesthetist and a hospital director who spent April writing to the ministry
about equipment, and we read their letters against the transfer dates.

The health unions gain a party that used their material rather than their
photograph. The government cannot answer it with a procedural defence, because
the argument is no longer procedural.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@vent20_scandal
title: Run it as a straight corruption attack
subtitle: The fastest route to coverage; it burns in a week and leaves nothing behind but the word "arms dealer".
on-arrival: {!
Q.procurement_scandal_stance = "Corruption attack";
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 2;
Q.media_capacity = (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) + 3;
Q.left_poll_momentum =
    (Number(Q.left_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.15;
Q.pis_relation = (Number(Q.pis_relation) || 0) - 6;
Q.institutional_trust = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) - 2
);
Q.covid_anti_system_pressure =
    (Number(Q.covid_anti_system_pressure) || 0) + 3;
Q.news_headline =
    "The ventilator contract becomes a straight corruption charge";
!}

Arms dealer, thirty-five million, no ventilators. Three facts, one sentence, a
week of coverage and a measurable bump.

It also feeds the growing conviction that the whole pandemic was a business
arrangement conducted over the public's head — a conviction that will be
harvested next year by people who are not us, and who will not stop at
procurement.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue
